      "id": "ch08_q04",
      "answer": "a. The 99% interval is $0.995\\pm2.576(0.02/\\sqrt{50})=[0.9877,1.0023]$ gallons.\n\nb. One gallon lies inside the interval, so the data do not show a statistically significant shortage at the 1% level.\n\nc. With $n=50$, the CLT makes the z interval reasonably robust; exact normality is not essential if the population is not extremely skewed.\n\nd. The 95% interval is $0.995\\pm1.96(0.02/\\sqrt{50})=[0.9895,1.0005]$, which also contains one gallon, so there is still no clear evidence of a shortage.",
