      "answer": "Use $n=z_{0.995}^2p(1-p)/E^2$ with $z_{0.995}=2.576$.\n\na. $n=2.576^2(0.05)(0.95)/0.02^2=787.9$, so $n=788$.\n\nb. $n=2.576^2(0.10)(0.90)/0.02^2=1492.9$, so $n=1493$.\n\nc. $n=2.576^2(0.05)(0.95)/0.05^2=126.1$, so $n=127$ to ensure the stated precision.",
