      "answer": "A critical value is a cutoff for a test statistic chosen so that the probability of falling in the rejection region under $H_0$ equals the significance level $\\alpha$. Reject $H_0$ when the observed statistic lies beyond the cutoff in the direction specified by $H_a$.",
