      "answer": "Let $H_0:\\mu_1-\\mu_2\\le0$ and $H_a:\\mu_1-\\mu_2>0$. The observed difference is 0.13 and $\\operatorname{SE}=\\sqrt{0.7^2/100+0.6^2/100}=0.0922$. Thus $z=0.13/0.0922=1.41$, with one-sided p-value $\\approx0.080$. Fail to reject $H_0$ at 0.05; the sample does not provide sufficient evidence that car ownership lowers GPA.",
